/-!
# Complex parameter estimates for ordered evolution

The ordered evolution is entire in its complex LCHS parameter and grows at most exponentially in
the magnitude of the imaginary part. Real-complex derivative compatibility and Cauchy estimates
then bound parameter derivatives for quadrature applications. See [AnChildsLin2026] for the
mathematical setting.

## Main statements

* `ordered_unitary_complex_parameter_growth`: Under the stated continuous Hermitian field and
  norm bounds, the complex-parameter ordered evolution has norm at most `Real.exp (|z.im| * T *
  Λ)` for `T ≥ 0`.
* `ordered_unitary_complex_parameter_entire`: For continuous matrix fields `L` and `H`, the
  ordered evolution generated by `Complex.I • (H u + z • L u)` is entire in `z`.
* `ordered_unitary_k_derivative_cauchy`: For any positive radius `R`, the `q`-th real parameter
  derivative of the ordered evolution has norm at most `q.factorial * Real.exp (R * T * Λ) /
  R^q` under the stated Hermitian and norm bounds.

## References

* [An, Childs, and Lin, 2026][AnChildsLin2026]
-/

